revisions (common.nix); none of it is copied into this repository. Each keeps its own licence.

- Indium and Iridium, https://github.com/darlinghq/indium (e3a1f2212bdadade0afe2e10728e7673f49d3c98)
  0BSD. Copyright (C) 2022 by Ella Stanforth; Copyright (C) 2022 Darling developers.
  Our change: patches/indium/0001 (0BSD, like the file it changes).
  The test programs built from it (indium-test-*) and their shader files (add.metallib, add-mslc.spv,
  add-mslc.reflect.json) are Indium's own test suite.
- darling-metal (Metal.framework), https://github.com/darlinghq/darling-metal
  (57a8a2d34685f34424b961182e45c2ff2642f37f): MPL-2.0 per file (LICENSES/ in that repository; some
  files CC0-1.0, ISC, MIT). Our changes to MPL-2.0 files are the substituteInPlace lines of metal.nix,
  published here and MPL-2.0 like the files they change. Nothing of the GPL-3.0 main Darling
  repository is used.
- mslc, https://github.com/darlinghq/mslc (6964bb3984e26de95bbca89b08f305a6c4ff3317): MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Cristian Magherusan-Stanciu. Unchanged.
- LLVM 21.1.8 (libLLVM.dylib, Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), as the PureDarwin flake builds it.

Ours (MIT): every other file here: the recipes, tools/, test/sf-metal-tri.m and test/sf-tri.metal
(our shaders), shim/ (our own declarations of what PureDarwin's headers lack; no Apple header was used).
No Apple-toolchain output of ours is used: the only precompiled metallibs are those in Indium's test
suite, and our shaders are compiled by mslc from our MSL source.
